<h2 style="margin: 0.0px 0.0px 14.9px 0.0px; font: 18.0px 'Helvetica Neue'; color: #0f6745; -webkit-text-stroke: #0f6745"><span class="s1"><b>Final Thoughts: Stay Cool (or Warm) Without Getting Burned</b></span></h2>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">HVAC replacement is one of the most significant home investments. The right system, properly installed, will serve you for 15-25 years.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">But the HVAC industry thrives on complexity and fear. Contractors know most homeowners don't understand tonnage, SEER ratings, or what installation should actually cost.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">You now know: - What equipment costs at each efficiency level - What installation labor should run - Where contractors commonly pad quotes - How to save money without sacrificing quality</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Get multiple quotes. Insist on Manual J load calculations. Verify equipment pricing. Ask questions.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1">Most HVAC contractors are honest professionals. But the ones who aren't are counting on your confusion.</span></p>
<p class="p2"><span class="s1"><b>Know your numbers. Buy smart.</b></span></p>
